9164-edit"},{"invocation":{"touched":["tests/userequire_spec.lua"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":"tests/userequire_spec.lua","before":"    ok(r == nil or r.class == 'host-root', 'no cross-file use to report: ' .. vim.inspect(r))","after":"    eq(nil, r, 'no cross-file use reaches the stub: nothing to classify (it was `host-root` while the call landed there)')"}},"verb":"edit","id":"1791235917.268200-edit"},{"invocation":{"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":" MEASURED on lua/cartograph/algebra's basis: pure 31 → 35 (locate_at, positions, spans, eq); the rest are held by a bare `key` read through the installer's second parameter (`SHARED.key`), a `table.sort` on a local made by a CALL, a fn-value `with_cursor`. Repo-wide: pure 2,104 → 2,109, writes 222 → 228 (callbacks' and continuations' real writes now inherited). `tests/fixpoint_spec.lua`. CART-1484, CART-1494, CART-1495 |","after":" ⚠ MEASURE OVER THE WHOLE TREE (`toolbelt run … lua`): a census rooted at a SUB-tree (`lua/cartograph/algebra`) resolves no `require('cartograph.…')`, so it sees no installer family and no cross-file link — it reads the code in isolation, and it also cannot see the false links that pollute the real graph. 2026-10-05, over lua/: false links were the largest source of `writes~` — an identifier argument that was the caller's PARAMETER linked to another file's function (CART-1498: core's `child(path, i)` → stampcache.lua's `path`, gluing core into a 53-member 16-file cycle with ir.lua), a stdlib call captured by another file's runtime override (CART-1499: `table.sort` → sort-ties.lua's), a part's `SHARED.key` unresolved (CART-1497). The algebra basis: 0 writes~ (was 14), 39 pure, 12 pure~ (named hedges: `table.sort` on a local made by a CALL, a fn-value `with_cursor`, `setmetatable` on an opaque arg), 3 io~. Repo-wide: pure 2,104 → 2,277, writes~ 2,644 → 1,691, the largest call cycle 53 → 18. `tests/fixpoint_spec.lua`. CART-1484, CART-1494, CART-1495, CART-1497, CART-1498, CART-1499 |"}},"verb":"edit","id":"1791236179.153461-edit"}],"explained":11425,"version":1,"entries":[{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","id":"1791235345.780223-edit","bytes":1242,"decided_by":"tactic","invocation":{"touched":["lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":"lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua","before":"                            local b = fa[name]\n                            if not b then fa[name] = { recv = arecv, member = amember, n = 1 }\n                            else b.n = b.n + 1 end\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end\n        -- header/interface elements (C/C++): prototypes, macros and types.","after":"                            local b = fa[name]\n                            if not b then fa[name] = { recv = arecv, member = amember, n = 1 }\n                            else b.n = b.n + 1 end\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n            elseif defn and namen and valn and spec.field_alias and spec.installer_scope and spec.installer_scope(defn) then\n                -- an INSTALLER part's body IS its module scope (CART-1497): `return function (M, SHARED) local key =\n                -- SHARED.key … end` — its field aliases are recorded like a file's own (and nothing else: no var node).\n                -- Once per name (seen_var: the vars query matches a multi-assignment's name once per value)\n                local name = node_text(namen, src)\n                local id = ('%s::alias:%s@%d'):format(file, name, pos_of(defn).start.line)\n                if not seen_var[id] then\n                    seen_var[id] = true\n                    local arecv, amember = spec.field_alias(valn, src)\n                    if arecv and amember then\n                        data.fieldalias = data.fieldalias or {}\n        